          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Representative Case Study"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A premium visual breakdown of how a failed injector tip scored a bore, and why a full rebuild at £4,000 was cheaper than buying a replacement Hilux."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“The Hilux started chugging white smoke at traffic lights. The idle was rough, like it was missing on one cylinder. Then the knock started — a deep, rhythmic thud from the engine bay. My mechanic pulled the injectors and said, ‘The tip’s gone on number three. It’s been bouncing around in there. The bore is scored.’ I thought my truck was scrap. But he said, ‘Mate, it’s a Hilux. We rebuild it. It’ll outlast you.’”"
        },
