    "initialSymptom": {
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "the-whole-disaster-started-with-white-smoke-at-traffic-lights",
          "title": "The whole disaster started with white smoke at traffic lights.",
          "description": "The owner noticed white smoke on cold starts, which worsened over several weeks. A rough idle and knocking followed. The 1KD-FTV injector tip had detached and was bouncing around inside the cylinder, scoring the bore.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/case-studies/assets/1.2-toyota-hilux-1kd-legend.png",
              "alt": "Toyota Hilux comparison - £4,000 rebuild vs £40,000 new Hilux",
              "width": "",
              "height": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "What owner thought"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "“Maybe it’s just a sensor”"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The truck still drove, so the symptom did not feel urgent."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "What it actually was"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Injector tip failure"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The tip detached, scored the bore, and damaged the piston crown."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Why it matters"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Scored bore = rebuild"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Once the bore is scored, the only fix is a re-bore and oversize pistons."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "If your 1KD-FTV develops white smoke, rough idle, or a knock, have the injectors tested immediately. A £200 injector test could save a £4,000 rebuild."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Failure timeline"
            }
          ],
          "links": [],
          "source": {
